# Python Conventions (New Code)

- Target Python 3.11+ style already used in the app (`str | None`, f-strings).
- Prefer pure functions for analysis/report building; keep Streamlit I/O at the edge.
- Type chart payloads with TypedDict / dataclasses in new `schemas/` when adding pipelines.
- Fail soft for optional AI: return `None` / skip section; never break PDF or chart render.
- Do not add heavy new dependencies without updating a **new** requirements overlay or documenting the pin; avoid changing existing `requirements.txt` unless asked.
- Tests: golden fixtures with known DOB/place expected sublords/dashas when touching interpretation helpers.
